# arch/os/windows/scan — where the system calls in a run of code are.
#
# Pure functions over a buffer: no system calls, no allocation, no state. The
# driver is this directory's; the step is the file named after the machine
# being built for, and on x86-64 that file is the Linux decoder compiled again
# with a Windows lookback in front (x86_64.c says why it is not a copy).
#
# Both machines Windows runs on are here, which is more than macOS has: on
# Windows the system calls are all in one image, ntdll, and every one of them is
# a stub of the same few instructions, so the question this answers has a
# precise answer and a reason to be asked. Nothing in this tree asks it yet —
# there is no sc/ here (see the platform README) and tools/ub-patch writes ELF.
obj-$(CONFIG_OS_SCAN) += scan.o $(ARCH).o
